# agent-prompts-safety

> **Purpose:** Keep the model controlled and the agent safe.
>
> **Applies to:** Prompts, nodes and the browser agent in `apps/api`.

## Structured output
- Use structured output with a Zod schema for every model call.
- Never parse free text from the model.
- Extract one guide section per call.
- Repair a failed section at most once, with the validation error. Then mark it Uncertain.

## Prompts
- Keep prompts in `src/agent/prompts/`, one file per stage.
- Every prompt allows "unknown" as an answer and forbids invented facts.
- Never put secrets or user data in prompts.

## Injection safety
- Treat fetched page text as data, never as instructions.
- Wrap page text in clear delimiters inside prompts.
- Tell the model to ignore instructions found in sources.
- Fetch only URLs from the search stage. Never follow links found in page text.

## Probe
- Send only a GET to the authorize URL, with a dummy client ID.
- Never submit forms or use real credentials.

## Browser agent
- Off unless `ENABLE_BROWSER_AGENT=true`.
- Runs locally only, never in the deployed app.
- Never store its credentials in the repo.
